# Cognition Benchmark Manufacturing

> ggen projection from `benchmark-manufacturing/ontology.ttl`. Do not hand-edit.

The benchmark court admits **{{ results[0]["expected"] }} canonical cognition breeds** from `BreedId::ALL`.

## Manufacture topology

`canonical cognition ontology -> DSPy SELECT -> deterministic admission -> ggen CONSTRUCT -> Divan/contract/docs -> execution -> receipt`

DSPy is allowed to explore benchmark designs. Its output is never executable by itself. Admission must preserve the canonical breed inventory and the anti-hiding lower bounds. ggen deterministically projects admitted law into repository-native benchmark surfaces. Neither tool receives DO authority.

## Anti-hiding matrix

Batch scales: {% for row in batches %}`{{ row["value"] }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.

Adversarial irrelevant-context scales: {% for row in noise %}`{{ row["value"] }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} facts.

Every breed is measured on `kernel_only` and `full_lifecycle`; every breed is also measured under context pressure. Allocation profiling and throughput counters are mandatory. Fixtures must be grounded, falsifiable, non-empty, and executable through both raw and lawful dispatch paths.

## Standing law

A prompt, DSPy prediction, RDF graph, ggen plan, rendered source file, queued workflow, or benchmark name is not a performance receipt. `ALIVE` requires execution of the exact admitted subject and independent verification that all canonical breeds and required measurement points are present.

`SELECT != CONSTRUCT != DO`; benchmark actuation remains `REFUSED`.
